How do I match a pattern instead of a literal word? String search terms are matched literally, so characters like (, ., or $ match themselves. To match a pattern, pass a RegExp search term (which is used as-is, with its own flags): import Highlighter from "react-highlight-words";

function RegExpExample() {
 return (
 <Highlighter
 searchWords={[/\$\d+\.\d{2}/]}
 textToHighlight="Was $12.99, today only $9.99"
 />
 );
} Alternatively, set the autoEscape prop to false to treat every string search term as a regular expression. Only do this for trusted search terms; a malicious regular expression can take an extremely long time to run.
